{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-07:g3_proxy:1","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"correlation-identity-split","locations":[{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":6968,"end_line":6981},{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":7241,"end_line":7273}],"mechanism_tags":["unstable_token","unstable_scope_key","repeated_effect"],"rationale":"Pending/completed checks use the raw stringified correlation value, while the monitor transition receives a separately, lossily coerced integer. Equivalent tokens such as \"01\" and 1 therefore occupy different deduplication keys but drive the same modeled identity, and distinct nonnumeric tokens can all become 0. Duplicate irreversible completions can consequently evade the at-most-once check or unrelated effects can collide.","severity":"high"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:75e9e58303b82df311ac0c0682d688fb61b600515e0b4794ac3ae6862b884e02","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:c17cfd2e50566f23b816456a804dbd9c605df78a25019906f2927e903adcd83e","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-identity-split"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:f5fca10a9f597697c653478c5eddb4a4bab305ddba1bd8eea1b91aed93a8384a","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-identity-split"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:3b5478a4aa68dad29f79b8aaab801bd4df4db17914286613159ccc08d13a3353","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-identity-split"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:9143afeb42824e030784abda21a074d7f4f792b119149ed6cf99bb9468103054","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-identity-split"]}]}